/* src/parse/codelang.def — [INLINE-C] stage 2 THE LANGUAGE TABLE of embedded
 * code (docs/design/inline_c.md §1.1, §2.2): one row per registered language
 * of the tagged `(?C` string (``(?C`c: ...`)``), the SINGLE SOURCE every
 * language fact is projected from.
 *
 *   PCREC_CODE_LANG(id, tag, feature, module)
 *
 *   id        a C identifier, pasted into the generated names (the
 *             registry row's recogniser, src/parse/registry.c)
 *   tag       the language tag as an author writes it before `:`/`,`
 *             (``(?C`c,once: ...`)``), `[a-z][a-z0-9_]*`
 *   feature   the module's FEAT_* bit (src/core/internal.h)
 *   module    the module name, `code-<tag>`, as diagnostics and
 *             `--list-syntax` spell it
 *
 * WHAT IS PROJECTED FROM A ROW: the registry row (owned by `module`,
 * RF_INVOKER_ONLY: the GRANT column, §5.1), the language list
 * `--allow-code` accepts (`pcrec_code_grant_resolve`, src/parse/enabled.c),
 * the tags the recogniser and the port read, and the `<PREFIX>_CODE_LANGS`
 * stamp's vocabulary. A later language adds ONE row here and its FEAT_*
 * bit in src/core/internal.h's feature enum (a second site, since the bit
 * is a module fact the registry owns; review 2026-10-27-r1-ic2 F30);
 * nothing else changes (§2.2's last paragraph). The `(?{ ... })` spelling, whose end needs
 * a per-language scanner column, is row [SCANNER-DOGFOOD]'s (ruling R1,
 * 2026-10-27), not this table's yet. */
PCREC_CODE_LANG(c, "c", FEAT_CODE_C, "code-c")
